215
01:25:51.138 --> 01:25:55.138
And at this moment, they all come together for dinner.

216
01:26:01.138 --> 01:26:03.138
It is a small foretaste of the kingdom.

217
01:26:07.138 --> 01:26:10.138
Raised from the dead at tables with Jesus.

218
01:26:12.138 --> 01:26:13.138
Delicious food.

219
01:26:21.138 --> 01:26:26.138
There they held a meal in honor of Him, of Jesus.

220
01:26:28.138 --> 01:26:29.138
Magda served.

221
01:26:33.138 --> 01:26:36.138
And Lazarus was one of the people who were reclining at the table with him.

222
01:26:41.138 --> 01:26:46.138
And Mary took a pound of very costly pure nard oil.

223
01:26:47.138 --> 01:26:51.138
She anointed the feet of Jesus.

224
01:26:54.138 --> 01:26:56.138
And wiped them with her hair.

225
01:27:00.138 --> 01:27:03.138
And the fragrance of the oil filled the whole house.

226
01:27:09.138 --> 01:27:14.138
But Judas Iscariot, one of the disciples who would later betray him, asked...

227
01:27:17.138 --> 01:27:23.138
Why was this oil not sold for 300 denarii and the money given to the poor?

228
01:27:25.138 --> 01:27:27.138
It was worth about a year's wages.

229
01:27:31.138 --> 01:27:34.138
He said this not because he cared about the poor.

230
01:27:36.138 --> 01:27:38.138
But because he was a thief.

231
01:27:41.138 --> 01:27:44.138
He had the money box and stole from it.

232
01:27:47.138 --> 01:27:51.138
But Jesus said, let her alone.

233
01:27:58.138 --> 01:28:00.138
She has kept this for the day of my burial.

234
01:28:03.138 --> 01:28:05.138
The poor you will always have with you.

235
01:28:07.138 --> 01:28:09.138
But you will not always have me in your midst.

236
01:28:09.138 --> 01:28:13.138
This is the moment just before the triumphal entry into Jerusalem.

237
01:28:19.138 --> 01:28:22.138
He has come to Bethany to find rest.

238
01:28:22.138 --> 01:28:27.138
And everyone is there. The disciples, a few good friends, everyone is there.

239
01:28:30.138 --> 01:28:31.138
Martha is there.

240
01:28:32.138 --> 01:28:34.138
And what does Martha do? She serves.

241
01:28:35.138 --> 01:28:36.138
She has not changed.

242
01:28:38.138 --> 01:28:39.138
She has not changed.

243
01:28:41.138 --> 01:28:42.138
She has not changed.

244
01:28:43.138 --> 01:28:44.138
She has not changed.

245
01:28:46.138 --> 01:28:47.138
She has not changed.

246
01:28:49.138 --> 01:28:50.138
She has not changed.

247
01:28:53.138 --> 01:28:54.138
She has not gone deeper.

248
01:28:55.138 --> 01:28:56.138
She is busy.

249
01:28:59.138 --> 01:29:01.138
She is near the Lord.

250
01:29:06.138 --> 01:29:09.138
But she misses every time exactly where it matters.

251
01:29:17.138 --> 01:29:21.138
In Luke 10 we read the story that Martha invites Jesus to her home.

252
01:29:23.138 --> 01:29:25.138
And Jesus comes and sits down.

253
01:29:28.138 --> 01:29:30.138
And for the rest of the evening, Martha is busy in the kitchen.

254
01:29:33.138 --> 01:29:37.138
And Jesus ultimately says, you are so busy and you let yourself be distracted by so many things.

255
01:29:42.138 --> 01:29:46.138
And it is not only about what she is doing, but especially the spirit that is in it.

256
01:29:46.138 --> 01:29:48.138
She is not only busy, she is distracted.

257
01:29:52.138 --> 01:29:54.138
And Martha represents many in the body of Christ.

258
01:29:59.138 --> 01:30:01.138
I have invited Jesus into my house and into my life.

259
01:30:03.138 --> 01:30:04.138
I know Jesus.

260
01:30:06.138 --> 01:30:07.138
But they do not see Him.

261
01:30:10.138 --> 01:30:11.138
They never go deeper.

262
01:30:11.138 --> 01:30:12.138
Always busy in His name.

263
01:30:15.138 --> 01:30:17.138
But when you talk to Him, there is no depth there.

264
01:30:25.138 --> 01:30:26.138
He wants you first.

265
01:30:31.138 --> 01:30:34.138
It's not, because in Luke 10, it's not, I will just be Martha.

266
01:30:34.138 --> 01:30:36.138
No, no, no, you are missing the point.

267
01:30:37.138 --> 01:30:41.138
And in the story in Luke 10, Jesus calls us to be like Mary, not like Martha.

268
01:30:46.138 --> 01:30:48.138
He says about Mary, she has chosen the better part.

269
01:30:51.138 --> 01:30:52.138
Mary sits at His feet.

270
01:30:54.138 --> 01:30:55.138
Mary listens to His words.

271
01:30:58.138 --> 01:31:00.138
You can enter the Christ in the kitchen of Christ.

272
01:31:01.138 --> 01:31:03.138
You can invite Christ into your life and never truly know Him.

273
01:31:25.138 --> 01:31:29.138
You can be saved, but do you not long for a deeper covenant with Jesus where you truly know Him and He knows you?

274
01:31:31.138 --> 01:31:34.138
Mary is continually presented to us as someone we may pursue.

275
01:31:43.138 --> 01:31:46.138
It's not about serving, it's about the heart behind it.

276
01:31:51.138 --> 01:31:57.138
And every time we encounter Mary of Bethany in the Word, she is sitting at the feet of the Lord.

277
01:31:58.138 --> 01:32:00.138
It is her heart for the Lord.

278
01:32:13.138 --> 01:32:19.138
Martha serves, Lazarus is sitting there and he is just happy to be there. I am here and I am alive.

279
01:32:22.138 --> 01:32:24.138
I am going to enjoy this moment with Jesus.

280
01:32:25.138 --> 01:32:27.138
But Mary becomes the focus again.

281
01:32:31.138 --> 01:32:32.138
Maria comes in humbly.

282
01:32:34.138 --> 01:32:36.138
It is her heart attitude towards the Lord.

283
01:32:37.138 --> 01:32:41.138
And somehow she does not fully know the week he is going to have.

284
01:32:42.138 --> 01:32:51.138
But because of the intimate union, I think she is attuned to what is temporary, what is right, and what is needed for the Lord.

285
01:33:06.138 --> 01:33:13.138
She has the revelation to anoint him with oil.

286
01:33:21.138 --> 01:33:30.138
She realizes that this moment of sharing a meal is an important moment and that Jesus needs her ministry.

287
01:33:37.138 --> 01:33:54.138
He did not need unrest around him, but he needed someone to come and see him and quietly minister to him.

288
01:33:55.138 --> 01:34:09.138
And as she breaks her jar and pours out the oil, she pours out a year's salary.

289
01:34:11.138 --> 01:34:12.138
What is that?

290
01:34:15.138 --> 01:34:19.138
Can you imagine throwing that entire year's salary into a collection basket?

291
01:34:20.138 --> 01:34:21.138
That is how much it was.

292
01:34:22.138 --> 01:34:23.138
It was precious.

293
01:34:28.138 --> 01:34:30.138
And she understood, he needs this moment.

294
01:34:35.138 --> 01:34:38.138
I want to give him something that costs me something.

295
01:34:38.138 --> 01:34:52.138
And it seems to me that many in the body of Christ never grasp this revelation.

296
01:34:53.138 --> 01:35:11.138
That there is a place in ministry to the Lord where he cares for your heart and that you can respond by caring for his heart.

297
01:35:13.138 --> 01:35:14.138
And then there is Judas.

298
01:35:16.138 --> 01:35:19.138
Judas has a totally different spirit within him.

299
01:35:19.138 --> 01:35:21.138
Judas has walked with the Lord for three years.

300
01:35:24.138 --> 01:35:25.138
He has been in the ministry.

301
01:35:27.138 --> 01:35:28.138
He has seen the miracles.

302
01:35:31.138 --> 01:35:32.138
He has sat at the table.

303
01:35:39.138 --> 01:35:44.138
And I don't know what it is, but there is something in his soul that has undergone a change at this moment.

304
01:35:49.138 --> 01:35:53.138
Do you know how people can be with you, but their heart is not with you?

305
01:35:56.138 --> 01:35:59.138
And it is sometimes difficult to be so distinctive.

306
01:36:01.138 --> 01:36:02.138
They are there, but they are not there.

307
01:36:05.138 --> 01:36:06.138
They are with you, but they are not with you.

308
01:36:07.138 --> 01:36:08.138
That is Judas.

309
01:36:12.138 --> 01:36:14.138
Judas has already lost his soul at this moment.

310
01:36:16.138 --> 01:36:17.138
But he has walked with the Lord for three years.

311
01:36:19.138 --> 01:36:20.138
He has sat at the table.

312
01:36:21.138 --> 01:36:22.138
He has given the food.

313
01:36:24.138 --> 01:36:25.138
He has heard the Word.

314
01:36:28.138 --> 01:36:29.138
What has happened to the soul of Judas?

315
01:36:31.138 --> 01:36:32.138
It is so tragic.

316
01:36:41.138 --> 01:36:45.138
He looks at what Mary gives to the Lord and he despises it.

317
01:36:50.138 --> 01:36:52.138
Jesus is very clear about Judas here.

318
01:36:53.138 --> 01:36:56.138
You say you care for the poor, but you have never given anything yourself.

319
01:36:59.138 --> 01:37:01.138
Where is then your money that you give to the poor?

320
01:37:06.138 --> 01:37:08.138
Why should the church have to build a building?

321
01:37:09.138 --> 01:37:11.138
Why should the church build a building?

322
01:37:12.138 --> 01:37:14.138
Why should the church build a building?

323
01:37:15.138 --> 01:37:17.138
Why should the church build a building?

324
01:37:17.138 --> 01:37:18.138
Why should the church build a building?

325
01:37:22.138 --> 01:37:24.138
But if you look at their account, they do not give.

326
01:37:27.138 --> 01:37:28.138
It is not real.

327
01:37:30.138 --> 01:37:31.138
There is a...

328
01:37:33.138 --> 01:37:34.138
Judas is real...

329
01:37:38.138 --> 01:37:39.138
Yes, a false spirit.

330
01:37:42.138 --> 01:37:43.138
Judas is fake.

331
01:37:48.138 --> 01:37:50.138
It is dark what is going on around Judas.

332
01:37:53.138 --> 01:37:54.138
Do not be a Judas.

333
01:37:57.138 --> 01:37:58.138
That is also what this story is about.

334
01:37:59.138 --> 01:38:00.138
Do not become a Judas.

335
01:38:06.138 --> 01:38:08.138
Have we all betrayed the Lord?

336
01:38:09.138 --> 01:38:10.138
Yes.

337
01:38:18.138 --> 01:38:20.138
But in the end, we do not want to be a Judas.

338
01:38:26.138 --> 01:38:32.138
Not every character we encounter in the Word is someone to pursue.

339
01:38:39.138 --> 01:38:43.138
You know, David sinned, so I can also just live in sin.

340
01:38:47.138 --> 01:38:51.138
I am still betrayed, so they can keep their patient agreement behind closed doors.

341
01:38:53.138 --> 01:38:54.138
People need to disappear.

342
01:39:02.138 --> 01:39:05.138
I am still betrayed, I can still minister to the people.

343
01:39:06.138 --> 01:39:08.138
No, God says that at some point.

344
01:39:14.138 --> 01:39:15.138
The time is coming.

345
01:39:18.138 --> 01:39:19.138
The time is coming.

346
01:39:21.138 --> 01:39:22.138
If you play games with God.

347
01:39:24.138 --> 01:39:25.138
He does not play games with you.

348
01:39:31.138 --> 01:39:33.138
He says, do what you need to do, brother.

349
01:39:38.138 --> 01:39:40.138
You have given up on me a long time ago.

350
01:39:41.138 --> 01:39:43.138
You have given up on me a long time ago.

351
01:39:52.138 --> 01:39:56.138
And there are people sitting in churches who have given up on the Lord a long time ago.

352
01:39:57.138 --> 01:39:59.138
And betray Him for money.

353
01:40:11.138 --> 01:40:12.138
Come on.

354
01:40:16.138 --> 01:40:20.138
The time is up, church, to play games in the house of the Lord.

355
01:40:20.138 --> 01:40:21.138
It is His house.

356
01:40:24.138 --> 01:40:28.138
He will bring things to light.

357
01:40:31.138 --> 01:40:34.138
Do not give up on the Lord for a quick fix.

358
01:40:41.138 --> 01:40:45.138
If you ask the Lord for work and He provides a job for you.

359
01:40:47.138 --> 01:40:51.138
And the next Sunday when it comes to giving, if you hold back, then you have a problem.

360
01:40:54.138 --> 01:40:57.138
We are all happy to receive the gifts of God.

361
01:41:03.138 --> 01:41:06.138
But if you truly believe that He provides for you.

362
01:41:07.138 --> 01:41:09.138
And you keep everything to yourself.

363
01:41:11.138 --> 01:41:12.138
What do you do then?

364
01:41:14.138 --> 01:41:15.138
Then you do not love Him.

365
01:41:19.138 --> 01:41:21.138
Then you use Him like a spirit in a bottle.

366
01:41:24.138 --> 01:41:26.138
And maybe it doesn't even come from Him.

367
01:41:32.138 --> 01:41:34.138
What he says is so true.

368
01:41:37.138 --> 01:41:43.138
Churches that never talk about money, the people are stuck to their money.

369
01:41:46.138 --> 01:41:48.138
We give and then it is free to talk about it.

370
01:41:50.138 --> 01:41:54.138
If you give, then you take no offense in talking about giving.

371
01:41:56.138 --> 01:41:58.138
Let us settle this with the heart.

372
01:42:02.138 --> 01:42:04.138
Where everything flows from.

373
01:42:07.138 --> 01:42:12.138
And he looks at Mary as if she has completely misunderstood, and Jesus says leave her alone.

374
01:42:22.138 --> 01:42:24.138
Mary has it right here.

375
01:42:24.138 --> 01:42:29.138
And a better translation would be, do not interrupt her, give her the freedom.

376
01:42:41.138 --> 01:42:43.138
Be no unreliable spirit.

377
01:42:46.138 --> 01:42:47.138
Give your own gift.

378
01:42:48.138 --> 01:42:49.138
Give your own life.

379
01:42:49.138 --> 01:42:50.138
Give your own life.

380
01:42:53.138 --> 01:42:56.138
Do not criticize others who give worship.

381
01:42:58.138 --> 01:43:00.138
Be busy with your own life.

382
01:43:07.138 --> 01:43:11.138
Because before you know it, you have wasted your life in criticism.

383
01:43:19.138 --> 01:43:22.138
Criticism of everything and everyone, and it is thrown away.

384
01:43:33.138 --> 01:43:34.138
We waste our time.

385
01:43:37.138 --> 01:43:39.138
If the Lord says be like Mary.

386
01:43:41.138 --> 01:43:42.138
Come to my feet.

387
01:43:49.138 --> 01:43:51.138
If it helps your posture.

388
01:43:51.138 --> 01:43:54.138
If it doesn't help, express how.

389
01:43:54.138 --> 01:43:57.138
To become a little humble before the Lord.

390
01:44:07.138 --> 01:44:10.138
Shouldn't we not waste our time?

391
01:44:12.138 --> 01:44:15.138
Shouldn't we not waste Sunday morning together?

392
01:44:15.138 --> 01:44:18.138
Shouldn't we not waste Sunday morning together?

393
01:44:18.138 --> 01:44:21.138
Let your eyes and look at the man on a cross.

394
01:44:21.138 --> 01:44:23.138
Stop looking at people.

395
01:44:23.138 --> 01:44:24.138
Look at the Lord.

396
01:44:25.138 --> 01:44:27.138
Please, I realize you.

397
01:44:27.138 --> 01:44:28.138
Look at him.

398
01:44:28.138 --> 01:44:30.138
Learn to become uncomfortable.

399
01:44:30.138 --> 01:44:32.138
Because you haven't done it in a long time.

400
01:44:32.138 --> 01:44:34.138
Or maybe you've never done it.

401
01:44:34.138 --> 01:44:35.138
And it is uncomfortable, the Lord.

402
01:44:35.138 --> 01:44:36.138
He says, I know it.

403
01:44:36.138 --> 01:44:37.138
But let us go there.

404
01:44:37.138 --> 01:44:40.138
Let us start digging a well together.

405
01:44:48.138 --> 01:44:51.138
Stop looking at others and look at Him.

406
01:45:09.138 --> 01:45:11.138
Jesus fully defends Mary here.

407
01:45:13.138 --> 01:45:14.138
What she does is right.

408
01:45:15.138 --> 01:45:17.138
What she does is at the right moment.

409
01:45:23.138 --> 01:45:26.138
Jesus says, you will always be able to serve the poor.

410
01:45:34.138 --> 01:45:36.138
But this moment is only once.

411
01:45:44.138 --> 01:45:48.138
When you read the gospel and there are small differences in perspective.

412
01:46:03.138 --> 01:46:07.138
When you read the gospel and there are small differences in perspective,

413
01:46:07.138 --> 01:46:11.138
as different people write an account of things that have happened,

414
01:46:11.138 --> 01:46:17.138
they all have their own perspective and that complements each other, it does not contradict each other.

415
01:46:37.138 --> 01:46:41.138
When you read the gospel and there are small differences in perspective,

416
01:46:41.138 --> 01:46:45.138
as different people write an account of things that have happened,

417
01:46:45.138 --> 01:46:49.138
they all have their own perspective and that contradicts each other.

418
01:47:07.138 --> 01:47:17.138
I think it is the gospel of Mark, where Jesus says to Mary, she gave what she could.

419
01:47:17.138 --> 01:47:24.138
And that is a special perspective, because sometimes we feel, what do we really have to offer?

420
01:47:24.138 --> 01:47:29.138
And Jesus says, you have given what you could and that was enough.

421
01:47:29.138 --> 01:47:38.138
In your life, you have given me what you could, and I receive it.

422
01:47:41.138 --> 01:47:46.138
The only moment when He cannot say that is when we hold it back.

423
01:47:47.138 --> 01:47:52.138
And Jesus gives the Messiah in this moment, He is about to enter Jerusalem as king.

424
01:47:52.138 --> 01:47:56.138
He says, she was going to keep it for my burial.

425
01:48:06.138 --> 01:48:11.138
But, and I thought about it, He does not remain dead.

426
01:48:12.138 --> 01:48:16.138
And through the spirit, she begins to give that oil.

427
01:48:16.138 --> 01:48:22.138
Jesus is about to enter Jerusalem as king and He will die, but He does not remain dead.

428
01:48:23.138 --> 01:48:27.138
Jesus will never deny our full dedication.

429
01:48:31.138 --> 01:48:33.138
Others may not understand it.

430
01:48:33.138 --> 01:48:35.138
Others will take criticism.

431
01:48:37.138 --> 01:48:40.138
But Jesus in heaven receives it.

432
01:48:42.138 --> 01:48:46.138
And that is the reason why Jesus receives it in heaven.

433
01:48:46.138 --> 01:48:48.138
Others will take criticism.

434
01:48:50.138 --> 01:48:54.138
But Jesus in heaven receives our full dedication.

435
01:49:08.138 --> 01:49:15.138
We come together to see Him. We do not come to see Tim or Vanessa, but we come together to behold Jesus.

436
01:49:17.138 --> 01:49:20.138
Together we want to see Him.

437
01:49:25.138 --> 01:49:29.138
Together we want to say, Lord, I have given today what I could.

438
01:49:38.138 --> 01:49:42.138
The choices that Mary makes in her life are an example for us.

439
01:49:47.138 --> 01:49:50.138
Jesus is blessed and then He enters Jerusalem.

440
01:50:05.138 --> 01:50:10.138
We read then, the next day there was already a large crowd in Jerusalem for the feast.

441
01:50:16.138 --> 01:50:21.138
And when they heard that Jesus would also come, they took palm branches and went out of the city to meet Him.

442
01:50:32.138 --> 01:50:37.138
As they cried out, Hosanna, blessed is He who comes in the name of the Lord, the King of Israel.

443
01:50:37.138 --> 01:50:42.138
This is the greatest festival in the Jewish calendar.

444
01:50:46.138 --> 01:50:48.138
This is not a crowd of thousands.

445
01:50:57.138 --> 01:51:00.138
It is a great, great Jewish feast.

446
01:51:00.138 --> 01:51:02.138
And it is not a small crowd that is there.

447
01:51:03.138 --> 01:51:11.138
We read in Josephus that at a Passover festival, 2, 2.5 million people travel to Jerusalem.

448
01:51:14.138 --> 01:51:17.138
And it is national hysteria.

449
01:51:32.138 --> 01:51:44.138
And when they say here, blessed is He who comes in the name of the Lord, they are quoting Psalm 118.

450
01:51:47.138 --> 01:51:52.138
And then they bring Him in as Messiah. They acknowledge that He is the Messiah.

451
01:51:55.138 --> 01:51:58.138
They say, You are the King of Israel.

452
01:52:02.138 --> 01:52:06.138
And at the end of the halal, they always take the palm branch.

453
01:52:06.138 --> 01:52:08.138
It is a sign.

454
01:52:08.138 --> 01:52:11.138
This is what they do in the millions.

455
01:52:15.138 --> 01:52:21.138
And it says, 14, Jesus found a young donkey. He sat on it, as it is written.

456
01:52:21.138 --> 01:52:25.138
Zechariah 9, it says, do not be afraid, daughter Zion.

457
01:52:25.138 --> 01:52:27.138
Do not be afraid, Jerusalem.

458
01:52:27.138 --> 01:52:30.138
Behold, your king comes to you.

459
01:52:30.138 --> 01:52:32.138
Blessed and humble, riding on a donkey.

460
01:52:32.138 --> 01:52:34.138
He does not come as you think.

461
01:52:34.138 --> 01:52:38.138
He does not come to deliver Israel from the Roman rules.

462
01:52:38.138 --> 01:52:42.138
He comes to deliver every human soul.

463
01:52:42.138 --> 01:52:46.138
From the grip of death, from hell and from the grave.

464
01:52:46.138 --> 01:52:48.138
That is what He comes to do.

465
01:52:48.138 --> 01:52:53.138
And Jesus does not come here as a mighty king to kick the Romans out.

466
01:52:53.138 --> 01:52:59.138
But He comes as a king who wants to redeem every person here.

467
01:52:59.138 --> 01:53:04.138
It says, Jesus saw a donkey standing, got on it, as it is written.

468
01:53:04.138 --> 01:53:09.138
Do not be afraid, Zion, your king is coming and he is sitting on a colt of a donkey.

469
01:53:15.138 --> 01:53:19.138
They have part of that revelation, but they do not have it fully.

470
01:53:24.138 --> 01:53:28.138
Yes, He comes, He brings everything that is prophesied.

471
01:53:28.138 --> 01:53:30.138
And He said, not entirely.

472
01:53:30.138 --> 01:53:32.138
Not entirely.

473
01:53:32.138 --> 01:53:33.138
Not yet.

474
01:53:45.138 --> 01:53:48.138
I am doing something much deeper in the earth.

475
01:53:48.138 --> 01:53:52.138
Jesus says, I am doing something here on earth that goes so much deeper.

476
01:53:59.138 --> 01:54:03.138
I am doing a deeper work for the soul of everyone who lives.

477
01:54:03.138 --> 01:54:06.138
In the past, in the present, in the future.

478
01:54:11.138 --> 01:54:16.138
It is not only for Israel, it is for Israel and to the ends of the earth.

479
01:54:19.138 --> 01:54:23.138
Together we will be saved, together we will sit at the table of the Lord.

480
01:54:23.138 --> 01:54:28.138
The Gentiles and the Jews together will sit at the wedding feast of the Lamb.

481
01:54:33.138 --> 01:54:37.138
He comes to remove the hostility of nationalistic joy.

482
01:54:37.138 --> 01:54:39.138
He says, Israel, I am coming to you slowly.

483
01:54:39.138 --> 01:54:41.138
I live for you.

484
01:54:41.138 --> 01:54:43.138
I am for you.

485
01:54:44.138 --> 01:54:46.138
He did not come for a nationalistic purpose.

486
01:54:46.138 --> 01:54:48.138
He came humbly.

487
01:54:48.138 --> 01:54:52.138
And he says, Israel, I come for you, but I do not come only for you.

488
01:54:57.138 --> 01:55:01.138
It is on the inside of every doomed soul.

489
01:55:01.138 --> 01:55:03.138
The kingdom of righteousness.

490
01:55:03.138 --> 01:55:07.138
It is on the inside of every doomed soul.

491
01:55:07.138 --> 01:55:10.138
It is on the inside of every doomed soul.

492
01:55:10.138 --> 01:55:17.138
The kingdom of righteousness, peace, and joy in the Holy Spirit.

493
01:55:28.138 --> 01:55:32.138
It is a kingdom that starts from the inside.

494
01:55:32.138 --> 01:55:35.138
It is a kingdom that starts from within.

495
01:55:41.138 --> 01:55:47.138
He saves souls to prepare them for the kingdom that will ultimately manifest physically.

496
01:55:49.138 --> 01:55:50.138
It is one-and.

497
01:55:52.138 --> 01:55:54.138
It is not one or the other.

498
01:55:58.138 --> 01:56:00.138
He cleanses a people from the inside out.

499
01:56:02.138 --> 01:56:03.138
Do you love Jesus?

500
01:56:07.138 --> 01:56:09.138
Do you obey Jesus?

501
01:56:11.138 --> 01:56:14.138
He says, if you love me, then you want to make me obedient.

502
01:56:16.138 --> 01:56:19.138
Perhaps we should start asking each other, are you obedient to Jesus?

503
01:56:21.138 --> 01:56:22.138
Why?

504
01:56:33.138 --> 01:56:39.138
That love is interpreted so broadly, but it is Jesus who determines what love is.

505
01:56:41.138 --> 01:56:42.138
Are you obedient to Him?

506
01:56:43.138 --> 01:56:44.138
Do you receive Him?

507
01:56:46.138 --> 01:56:48.138
Have you received His first coming?

508
01:56:48.138 --> 01:57:00.138
Have you submitted faith that your own soul receives the cleansing work before your death, that you cannot relax without a mediator?

509
01:57:01.138 --> 01:57:04.138
Someone had to stand in His place.

510
01:57:04.138 --> 01:57:15.138
Have you confessed that you yourself need a savior for your own sin, that you need a mediator, that you needed someone to stand in your place?

511
01:57:34.138 --> 01:57:56.138
We need Christ so much. The price of our sin is still death, unless we believe Him at His word and accept His sacrifice.

512
01:57:57.138 --> 01:58:05.138
He is the king, but He is the king in the whole universe.

513
01:58:10.138 --> 01:58:13.138
Let us stand. Let us pray.

514
01:58:19.138 --> 01:58:22.138
They sing it so loudly, Hosanna.

515
01:58:26.138 --> 01:58:31.138
And a week later many of them will shout, crucify Him.

516
01:58:57.138 --> 01:59:09.138
It is sad to first shout Hosanna and then shout crucify Him. We need a deeply rooted system.

517
01:59:11.138 --> 01:59:21.138
Even the one who was closest to Him did not fully understand until it happened.

518
01:59:26.138 --> 01:59:31.138
We must go deep into our Messiah, whom we love and pray so loudly.

519
01:59:32.138 --> 01:59:36.138
Let us make sure that you still do it in four years.

520
01:59:37.138 --> 01:59:41.138
In five years you did not enter it for the world and for the grief and you lost your soul.

521
01:59:42.138 --> 01:59:44.138
Be convinced that you know what you are saying.

522
01:59:45.138 --> 01:59:49.138
Be convinced that during this Holy Week you are looking at the glorious sling.

523
01:59:50.138 --> 01:59:52.138
Look to Him. Go to Him.

524
01:59:52.138 --> 01:59:57.138
Look to Jesus. Use this week to let your roots grow deep in Him.

525
01:59:58.138 --> 02:00:04.138
Grow in your awareness of who He is and perhaps we do not understand the full picture on this side,

526
02:00:05.138 --> 02:00:08.138
but let us do our best to see Him for who He truly is.

527
02:00:10.138 --> 02:00:13.138
Lord, I pray for us.

528
02:00:13.138 --> 02:00:16.138
That we will be a people who know You.

529
02:00:18.138 --> 02:00:19.138
To know You.

530
02:00:20.138 --> 02:00:21.138
From the inside out.

531
02:00:24.138 --> 02:00:28.138
Let us not be a people who only look at external things.

532
02:00:33.138 --> 02:00:37.138
Let us not be a people who only look at external things.

533
02:00:38.138 --> 02:00:43.138
I pray that we will have a deep friendship and a deep knowing of Jesus

534
02:00:44.138 --> 02:00:48.138
who has come, who was slain, and who has risen again.

535
02:00:57.138 --> 02:01:00.138
Spend your time getting to know Him.

536
02:01:01.138 --> 02:01:02.138
Give what you can.

537
02:01:03.138 --> 02:01:04.138
And He will receive it.

538
02:01:05.138 --> 02:01:09.138
Spend your time getting to know Him.

539
02:01:11.138 --> 02:01:12.138
Give what you can.

540
02:01:14.138 --> 02:01:15.138
And He will receive it.

541
02:01:18.138 --> 02:01:19.138
Look.

542
02:01:24.138 --> 02:01:26.138
Do not look at others.

543
02:01:26.138 --> 02:01:35.138
Do not look at others, but look at your own life and give what you can give to Him.

544
02:01:35.138 --> 02:01:38.138
And He will receive that, how beautiful is the Lord.

545
02:01:49.138 --> 02:01:54.138
It is so important that you accept Jesus now as the Lamb that was slain.

546
02:01:56.138 --> 02:01:58.138
I will wait for a few people.

547
02:01:58.138 --> 02:02:02.138
If there is anyone who says he needs to kill himself with his mouth.

548
02:02:02.138 --> 02:02:07.138
Jesus is Lord and I receive the work He did for me.

549
02:02:07.138 --> 02:02:09.138
In my place.

550
02:02:09.138 --> 02:02:10.138
Remember that He was innocent.

551
02:02:10.138 --> 02:02:12.138
It is you on that cross.

552
02:02:12.138 --> 02:02:13.138
It is you, it is me.

553
02:02:13.138 --> 02:02:15.138
That is what He does.

554
02:02:15.138 --> 02:02:18.138
So Lord, if you are that person this morning,

555
02:02:18.138 --> 02:02:20.138
then I am just going to invite you to come here.

556
02:02:20.138 --> 02:02:22.138
I may have two or three leaders standing.

557
02:02:22.138 --> 02:02:25.138
To help you talk that through.

558
02:02:25.138 --> 02:02:29.138
If you want to confess with your mouth this morning that you need Jesus,

559
02:02:29.138 --> 02:02:32.138
that you realize that He died in your place.

560
02:02:32.138 --> 02:02:38.138
Then come forward and pray with someone who is here.

561
02:02:38.138 --> 02:02:41.138
Be saved today.

562
02:02:41.138 --> 02:02:43.138
Lord, we love You.

563
02:02:48.138 --> 02:02:52.138
May we be a people that learns to love You more and more.

564
02:02:56.138 --> 02:02:59.138
Thank you, Vanessa and Rachel.

565
02:02:59.138 --> 02:03:03.138
So good to hear pure words from God.

566
02:03:08.138 --> 02:03:11.138
This was not a sermon to gain wisdom.

567
02:03:11.138 --> 02:03:14.138
This was a call to action.

568
02:03:14.138 --> 02:03:16.138
A call to get to work.

569
02:03:16.138 --> 02:03:18.138
God is calling clearly.

570
02:03:18.138 --> 02:03:20.138
God is calling us as an open church.

571
02:03:20.138 --> 02:03:25.138
And God is calling us individually to go deeper this week.

572
02:03:25.138 --> 02:03:27.138
We have a choice.

573
02:03:27.138 --> 02:03:29.138
We can be like Martha.

574
02:03:29.138 --> 02:03:30.138
Always busy.

575
02:03:30.138 --> 02:03:31.138
Doing all sorts of things.

576
02:03:31.138 --> 02:03:33.138
The day is gone so quickly.

577
02:03:33.138 --> 02:03:36.138
You can also choose to be like Mary.

578
02:03:36.138 --> 02:03:38.138
And truly take time for Him.

579
02:03:38.138 --> 02:03:41.138
Not just quickly, not because it has to be done.

580
02:03:41.138 --> 02:03:44.138
But sitting at Jesus' feet.

581
02:03:44.138 --> 02:03:46.138
And seek Him.

582
02:03:46.138 --> 02:03:49.138
Shall we do that this week?

583
02:03:50.138 --> 02:03:53.138
In Gethsemane, Jesus said to Peter.

584
02:03:53.138 --> 02:03:55.138
Can you not watch with me for one hour?

585
02:03:55.138 --> 02:03:57.138
And I have a challenge for you.

586
02:03:57.138 --> 02:03:58.138
And it should not be.

587
02:03:58.138 --> 02:04:04.138
But what if you take an hour for Jesus every day this week?

588
02:04:04.138 --> 02:04:07.138
Maybe you think, oh an hour, I can't do that.

589
02:04:07.138 --> 02:04:10.138
After ten minutes, I fall silent.

590
02:04:10.138 --> 02:04:13.138
Maybe that's actually a good thing once in a while.

591
02:04:13.138 --> 02:04:15.138
Mary paid a price.

592
02:04:15.138 --> 02:04:18.138
A very high price indeed.

593
02:04:18.138 --> 02:04:21.138
Maybe we should also pay a price once in a while.

594
02:04:21.138 --> 02:04:25.138
To not do the easy and the obvious for a moment.

595
02:04:25.138 --> 02:04:28.138
But to take real time for Him.

596
02:04:28.138 --> 02:04:30.138
Maybe you find it very difficult.

597
02:04:30.138 --> 02:04:33.138
But maybe that's actually really cool once in a while.

598
02:04:33.138 --> 02:04:36.138
Maybe God is waiting for you to fall silent for once.

599
02:04:36.138 --> 02:04:42.138
Maybe God is waiting for you to take real time for once.

600
02:04:42.138 --> 02:04:45.138
And it's okay if it falls silent for a moment.

601
02:04:45.138 --> 02:04:48.138
You can read multiple chapters in the Bible.

602
02:04:48.138 --> 02:04:50.138
You can let Him fall silent.

603
02:04:50.138 --> 02:04:52.138
You can pray in new tongues.

604
02:04:52.138 --> 02:04:53.138
You can worship Him.

605
02:04:53.138 --> 02:04:55.138
You can add a worship.

606
02:04:55.138 --> 02:04:56.138
You can do so much.

607
02:04:56.138 --> 02:04:58.138
But it shouldn't be forced.

608
02:04:58.138 --> 02:05:00.138
But at least.

609
02:05:00.138 --> 02:05:02.138
Every day this week.

610
02:05:02.138 --> 02:05:04.138
Go seek Him.

611
02:05:04.138 --> 02:05:05.138
He is waiting for you.

612
02:05:05.138 --> 02:05:07.138
He loves you so much.

613
02:05:07.138 --> 02:05:09.138
You are His joy.

614
02:05:09.138 --> 02:05:11.138
And He longs for you.

615
02:05:12.138 --> 02:05:16.138
We have the cards.

616
02:05:16.138 --> 02:05:19.138
Cross love.

617
02:05:19.138 --> 02:05:22.138
They are over there.

618
02:05:22.138 --> 02:05:24.138
So take some if you don't have any yet.

619
02:05:24.138 --> 02:05:26.138
Distribute them this week.

620
02:05:26.138 --> 02:05:27.138
Tell people.

621
02:05:27.138 --> 02:05:30.138
Do you actually know what Good Friday is about?

622
02:05:30.138 --> 02:05:32.138
Do you actually know what Easter is about?

623
02:05:32.138 --> 02:05:34.138
Do you know what happens at the cross?

624
02:05:34.138 --> 02:05:36.138
Then give them a card.

625
02:05:36.138 --> 02:05:38.138
Tell them about Jesus.

626
02:05:38.138 --> 02:05:40.138
About the cross and the resurrection.

627
02:05:40.138 --> 02:05:42.138
If they are interested.

628
02:05:42.138 --> 02:05:46.138
Tomorrow evening worship and prayer.

629
02:05:46.138 --> 02:05:48.138
A new beginning.

630
02:05:48.138 --> 02:05:51.138
Friday at half past seven.

631
02:05:51.138 --> 02:05:53.138
Gathering.

632
02:05:58.138 --> 02:06:01.138
Evangelism training tomorrow.

633
02:06:01.138 --> 02:06:02.138
Good.

634
02:06:02.138 --> 02:06:05.138
On Friday at half past seven we are going to celebrate Good Friday.

635
02:06:05.138 --> 02:06:07.138
We are going to worship Jesus.

636
02:06:07.138 --> 02:06:08.138
Good week everyone.

637
02:06:08.138 --> 02:06:10.138
Go deep with Him.
